      "writtenOn": "2023-11-07T08:41:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From what I understand of the documentation at go/android-flags-howto-apis and some YAQs answers, this annotation does not modify runtime behavior at all.\n\nThe recommended path is to always check that this flag is enabled before calling such an API -- _Ideally_ ART should throw an exception when an API is called when the flag is disabled, but it doesn\u0027t... so it is left upto the caller to manage any indeterminate state that may exist when the flag is disabled and the API is called.\n\nSo I think I can just add this check to other flag checks in the calling code and be fine. But I think I will still try to roll this out as fast as possible.",
